<title>BRAZIL: HSBC to assume Bamerindus foreign obligations.</title>
<headline>HSBC to assume Bamerindus foreign obligations.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong &amp; Shanghai Banking Corp will assume and honor all of Brazil's Bamerindus international obligations after a takeover deal, said Central Bank International Affairs director Gustavo Franco.</p>
<p>Franco said the only change under the new regime would be that Bamerindus' branches in New York, London and Luxembourg will be transferred to federal bank Banco do Brasil.  </p>
<p>&quot;All international obligations of Bamerindus of Brazil will be fully honored by the new owners of the bank,&quot; Franco told reporters.</p>
<p>He said the assets and liabilities of Bamerindus' branches in New York, London and Luxembourg will be fully honored by Banco do Brasil.</p>
<p>Banco do Brasil will receive a special credit line to support the transfer of those assets and liabilities.</p>
<p>((-- Michael Christie, Brasilia Newsroom, 5511 223 0358))</p>
